---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import { sections, identity } from '../data/content.js';

const s = sections.building;
---

<Page
  title="TailYield · Greg Jones"
  description="TailYield tells a private aircraft owner what a specific charter trip is actually worth to them, before they say yes."
  ogImage="/og/building.png"
  heading="Building"
  lede="TailYield."
>
  <div class="prose">
    {s.body.map((p) => <p>{p}</p>)}

    <p>
      <a href={s.cta.href} rel="noopener" target="_blank">{s.cta.label}</a>
    </p>

    <h2>Why it exists</h2>
    <p>
      Charter decisions get made on a quoted revenue figure. That figure is the operator's side of
      the trade. It says nothing about what the flight costs the owner in maintenance exposure,
      positioning, and schedule, which is the only side the owner actually pays for.
    </p>
    <p>
      The same division of labor applies here as everywhere else in the operation. The system
      assembles the numbers and shows its work. The owner decides.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about TailYield, or anything else: <a href={`mailto:${identity.email}`}>{identity.email}</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</Page>
